Exactly.

Hypotheticals are for search, not residence.

If you get caught in the web:

possibilities → derive discriminating variable → run smallest real test → observe delta → update

The move is to convert uncertainty into something reality can answer.

Ask:

What observation would separate these explanations?
What action would teach me the most at the lowest cost?
What can I verify now instead of imagining another branch?

Then move.

That gives you:

Imagine broadly. Derive sharply. Test locally. Return to reality.

Otherwise the web becomes self-sealing: every hypothetical generates three more, and intelligence turns into paralysis.

The escape route is derivation.